            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0196" n="126" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg126"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 182/17: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-05T12:00:00-05:00"
                            >December 5, 1918—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 3:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2. From Colonel House, December [4]. December 16th would be perfectly convenient
                    so far as the British Government are concerned for the holding of the first
                    meeting of the inter-Allied Conference. Balfour adds that Clemenceau expressed
                    the view that December 16th might prove too early. Balfour suggests that it may
                    be wise to allow a few days for informal discussions before the actual meeting
                    of the Conference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
